<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Segnespass and Segnesboden traverse — Tschinglenalp–Segnespass–Segnesboden–Alp Nagens [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From the actual Nideren/Tschinglenalp walking junction, ascend the marked path to Segnespass, descend the protected metal stairs, then follow the southern Atlas fork and upper Segnesboden western rim/outlet to lower Segnesboden, Segneshütte and the actual Alp Nagens walking endpoint.

T3 demanding mountain walking: steep ascent, loose rubble, an exposed pass descent and protected metal stairs/chains require sure-footedness. Mapped protection and bridges do not establish their current condition. Choose dry, snow-free ground, daylight and good visibility; snow, ice, fog and poor weather can make passage hazardous. Carry suitable mountain equipment and a map/compass; follow current signs and closures.

Stay on the marked walking course across the protected lower Segnesboden mire and floodplain; avoid trampling vegetation or disturbing wildlife. Alp Nagiens wildlife quiet zone has a legally binding foot and winter-sport entry closure from December 20 through April 30. This summer variant does not authorize winter passage. Current local restrictions govern.

Plan for summer, preferably late July–September after snow clears. Check transport and facility schedules separately; no operating lift, bus, hut or restaurant is promised.

Approximately 10.6 km. The 1,137 m ascent, 691 m descent and 255-minute duration are retained approximate legacy planning estimates, without surveyed heights or an elevation profile. This two-dimensional line is for planning, not navigation or an assurance of safety.

